# Frontend

- Default to Server Components; `"use client"` only for interactivity (forms, motion, video controls).
- Keep sections focused: one purpose, one headline, short supporting copy (campaign UX).
- Props: `Readonly<{ ... }>`. Prefer typed props over loose objects.
- Match existing export style in the file you touch (many components use `export default` today). New shared utilities: named exports.
- Tailwind for layout/spacing; reuse classes/tokens from `src/styles/globals.css` before inventing new ones.
- Icons: existing `src/components/Icons.tsx` or `lucide-react`.
- Images: prefer Next `<Image>` for static photos; hero video follows `heroMedia` contract in `src/data/site.ts`.
- No nested ternaries in JSX. No `any`. No non-null `!` — narrow instead.
- Don't add `useMemo` / `useCallback` unless the file already relies on them for a measured reason.
- Motion: intentional, few; don't sprinkle animation everywhere.
